---
description: What this repository records as open, and what each chart declares. Start every session here.
---

Run:

```bash
asgard-cli question
asgard-cli request
asgard-cli task
asgard-cli project
```

Read the questions first, so that you do not design past a question somebody
already knew was open.

None of these commands reports a position. Each prints a file the repository
keeps, or the CR kinds a chart declares. Nothing infers a step from them,
because an onboarding is not linear and an engagement can do things in any
order. You can read more than these four: `AGENTS.md`,
the living spec under `docs/spec/`, and what the customer said an hour ago.

Each project is listed with its shape, what its chart declares, and what it
still lacks in CR kinds. Under that, the guidance this repository's state
raises, each with the condition that raised it, so you can dismiss one whose
condition you know does not apply. None of it is a step you are at.

To reach guidance by subject instead:

```bash
grep -ril "<what you are actually deciding>" .agents/skills/asgard-platform/
```
